","body":"Through its subsidiary Helios Sustainable Energy Limited (95.24% held, acquired during FY26 for Rs.100 lacs investment), the Company plans a green-field Solar Power Panel manufacturing facility in Jodhpur, Rajasthan. Land identification is in progress with Government of Rajasthan support; the Company targets project completion by end of FY2026-27 and plant commissioning by end of Q1 FY2027-28. Separately, the Company is planning to re-enter raw-sugar import/export trading.","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"risks":{"title":"Risks (RHP)","body":"- Multiple pending legal cases filed by Mr. Ch. Krishna Murthy against the Company (and by the Company against him), including a suit seeking injunction on a past postal ballot for sale/transfer of the Company's Sugar business, a Section 9 Arbitration Act petition seeking a Receiver/Auditor, and an NCLT Company Petition relating to transfer of assets to Natems Sugar Private Limited; outcomes cannot be ascertained.\n- Auditors state the Company did not follow Ind AS 101 conversion provisions at transition date and could not determine the consequential impact; advances and various asset/liability balances remain subject to confirmation/reconciliation; multiple inter-balance transfers were carried out without proper confirmations or agreements from counterparties, so correctness, completeness and recoverability could not be commented upon.\n- Unredeemed 16% Cumulative Redeemable Preference Shares issued to promoters in 1995-97 (pending redemption since the Company's BIFR registration), with the eventual liability including accumulated dividend yet to be ascertained under modified SEBI rules.\n- An Income Tax claim for A.Y. 2013-14 is under appeal, and a Central Excise/GST demand confirming recovery of Service Tax (plus interest and penalty) on GTA services availed during 2005-2009 is under appeal before the Commissioner (Appeals); outcomes remain uncertain.\n- The Company's planned green-field Solar Power Panel manufacturing facility (via subsidiary Helios Sustainable Energy Limited) is a new line of business outside its existing sugar-trading expertise, with land yet to be identified and the project still in the planning stage.\n- The planned re-entry into raw-sugar import/export trading is contingent on the Government of India's recent duty-free import permission and prevailing industry inventory conditions, both of which are outside the Company's control.","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"strategy":{"title":"Strategies (RHP)","body":"- Embark upon fresh investments for expansion and growth of the existing trading business, including investments in subsidiaries and other new acquisitions if found feasible, and explore new initiatives into diverse areas of business including venturing into Green Energy as a green-field project.\n- Re-enter into import/export of raw sugar following the Government of India's permission for duty-free raw sugar imports for refining and domestic sale.","src":"drhp","as_of":""}},"scorecard":{},"concallIntel":{},"segments":[],"themes":[],"ipo":{"summary":{},"analysis":{}},"coverage":{"concall":false,"deepDive":false,"drhp":true,"projection":false,"stage":false},"pageModel":{"schemaVersion":"company-page/1.0","layout":"vertical","identity":{"symbol":"PRUDMOULI","name":"PRUDENTIAL SUGAR CORPORAT","sector":"Fast Moving Consumer Goods","industry":"Agricultural Food & other Products"},"coverage":{"deepDive":false,"drhp":true,"stage":false,"priceHistory":true,"themes":false,"concall":false},"adapters":{"deepDive":{"available":false,"profile":"none","sections":{}},"drhp":{"available":true,"structured":true,"profile":"drhp","sections":{"case":true,"business":true,"financials":true,"execution":false,"ownership":true,"risks":true,"peers":true,"listing":false,"verdict":false}}},"hero":{"oneLiner":"A Hyderabad-based company trading in Sugar and its allied products, now diversifying into Green Energy through a subsidiary.","businessQuality":null,"sector":"Fast Moving Consumer Goo